== a dialect error inside a function reports once
-c:2:6: error: The [[ conditional is a bash extension.
== each dialect use is reported
-c:2:7: error: The C-style for ((...)) loop is a bash extension.
-c:3:9: error: The C-style for ((...)) loop is a bash extension.
-c:7:9: error: The <<< here-string is a bash extension.
== an orphan after a closed command is reported
-c:1:4: error: The [[ conditional is a bash extension.
-c:4:1: error: 'fi' has no matching 'if'.
== an error outside any command keeps every later error
-c:1:1: error: The [[ conditional is a bash extension.
-c:2:1: error: 'fi' has no matching 'if'.
-c:3:1: error: 'done' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
== every error inside one body is reported
-c:2:10: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
-c:3:10: error: ';;' is only valid between the arms of a 'case'.
-c:5:1: error: Expected a command after '&&'.
-c:6:1: error: 'fi' has no matching 'if'.
== an unindented body recovers the same way
-c:3:8: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
-c:5:8: error: ';;' is only valid between the arms of a 'case'.
-c:7:1: error: '}' has no matching '{'.
== a closer of the enclosing command ends an unclosed if
-c:2:3: error: This 'if' has no closing 'fi'.
-c:7:3: error: ')' has no matching '('.
== a mismatched closer ends an unclosed loop
-c:2:3: error: This loop has no closing 'done'.
-c:5:1: error: 'done' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
== an unclosed case ends at the closing brace
-c:2:3: error: This 'case' has no closing 'esac'.
-c:5:1: error: '}' has no matching '{'.
== a header error skips its command by matched closers
-c:2:1: error: Expected an unquoted 'in' after the case word.
-c:4:1: error: 'esac' has no matching 'case'.
== keywords and braces as arguments do not close a command
-c:2:32: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
-c:4:1: error: 'done' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
== case patterns inside a skipped command do not close it
-c:2:3: error: Expected an unquoted 'in' after the case word.
-c:3:1: error: 'fi' has no matching 'if'.
== a heredoc body inside a failed statement is skipped
-c:2:13: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
-c:7:1: error: 'fi' has no matching 'if'.
== a quoted heredoc delimiter and a multi-line string
-c:6:5: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
-c:8:1: error: '}' has no matching '{'.
== an unterminated command at the end reports once
-c:2:3: error: This 'if' has no closing 'fi'.
== elif and else branches recover inside the if
-c:3:11: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
-c:6:8: error: ';;' is only valid between the arms of a 'case'.
-c:8:1: error: 'done' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
== each failed function reports its own error
-c:2:23: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
-c:5:23: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
== a subshell and a brace group inside a body
-c:2:20: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
-c:4:1: error: '}' has no matching '{'.
== deeply nested constructs report only the real error
-c:6:32: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
-c:12:1: error: '}' has no matching '{'.
== a missing then reports the if instead of its fi
-c:1:1: error: This 'if' has no 'then'.
-c:2:1: error: This loop has no 'do'.
== independent errors after a failed command are reported
-c:2:6: error: The condition before 'then' is empty.
-c:4:6: error: The condition before 'then' is empty.
-c:6:8: error: ';;' is only valid between the arms of a 'case'.
-c:8:1: error: '}' has no matching '{'.
== a missing do inside a function ends at the brace
-c:2:3: error: This loop has no 'do'.
-c:4:6: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
== an empty body keeps the errors after it
-c:1:15: error: The body after 'then' is empty.
-c:3:1: error: 'done' has no matching 'while', 'until', or 'for'.
-c:4:7: error: The brace group between '{' and '}' is empty.
-c:5:1: error: 'esac' has no matching 'case'.
== nested commands ended by one foreign closer report the innermost
-c:1:21: error: This loop has no closing 'done'.
-c:2:1: error: 'fi' has no matching 'if'.
== a keyword taken as an argument is pointed out at the end
-c:1:1: error: This 'if' has no closing 'fi'.
-c:1:20: details:
== a script file recovers the same way
3:10: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
7:1: error: 'fi' has no matching 'if'.
== lint reports every error in a file
2:10: error: Expected a command after the pipe to receive the output.
3:10: error: ';;' is only valid between the arms of a 'case'.
6:3: error: This 'if' has no closing 'fi'.
